@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# HANDOFF: races (package R of the hill content, phase 3)
+
+Request (Sachin): "Build the content, and then the tunnels and bridges", then "phase 3 (races, stunt jumps, cycling, parachuting, bungee)".
+Branch worktree-agent-a8e49a24b2d9859ff. Not pushed. Four shared files are NOT edited here: apply HANDOFF-races.patch.
+
+## What exists
+- `game/scripts/races.gd` (Node3D, `Races.new(); races.game = main; add_child(races)`). API: `prompt()` -> `[text, button]` or `[]`, `try_interact()` -> bool, `hud_text()`, `map_markers()`, `to_save()` / `load_save(d)` (best times day/night/bike, bike medal).
+- `game/scripts/race_course.gd`: static `hill(country, laps)` and `trail(country)`; builds the course at runtime from `game.city.country.roads`.
+- `game/tests/race_tests.gd` (15 tests, in TEST_MODULES), `race_shots.gd/.tscn` (8 shots).
+- `HANDOFF-races.patch`: the wiring for main.gd, hud.gd, player.gd, mission_manager.gd (`git apply --3way HANDOFF-races.patch`; checked with `git apply --check` on HEAD).
+
+## Design (decisions)
+- Day race: RACE_ROADS (East Hills Road, Whistler Track, Copperback Cut, Copperback Track) south of RACE_NORTH -3340, start by (2780, -2520). Route = 2-core ring of those roads plus a lead-in, sampled every 4 m and smoothed. 2 laps, a checkpoint about every 150 m, lap lines and the finish on one spot (ring junction, 136 m along the lead-in); the start arch stands 34 m along the lead-in.
+- Offered whenever it is not night (04:00 to 21:00). E near the start line starts the race instead of exiting the car (the patch puts races before exit). Prize 400 / 200 / 80 by place. Best time saved.
+- Night race 21:00 to 04:00 only: wager 100 to 500 (set_wager), winner takes the pot, faster rivals, one wanted star if a police unit sees you racing (police_manager's `_anyone_sees` rule: 35 m, ray on the world layer).
+- Rivals: 3 AI cars on `Vehicle.drive_path` (every 3rd route sample, corner speed profile v = sqrt(5 / curvature), brake 5.5). They ghost each other (collision exceptions plus `_ahead` ray exceptions, `_ghost_rivals`) so they never shunt the field; the player's car is solid. Day skills 0.86 / 0.9 / 0.95, night 1.0 / 1.05 / 1.1.
+- Rival recovery: waypoint skip when one is passed within 16 m; stall 5 s, 3 s off the line by 30 m, or no new route progress for 7 s (`IDLE_TIME`) puts the car back on the line (`recover_rival`); a wrecked rival is swapped for a fresh car at its path index.
+- Checkpoints count within 12 m (bike 11 m), in order; a skipped one does not count. Player abandons after 90 s without a checkpoint or 8 s out of the car.
+- Bike trial: Calder Trail downhill, $10 rental stand (3 bikes) at BIKE_SPOT (990, -1502), medals by average speed 4.6 / 5.6 / 6.6 m/s, cash 60 / 150 / 300 paid once per improvement, best time saved. Pace from an AI perfect run of 99 s.
+
+## Calibration (race_calib probe, deleted)
+- Day rivals average 15.8 to 17 m/s over the course; night 18 to 20 m/s. Ghost cars at skill 1.15 to 1.3 reach 20 to 22 m/s without crashing, so a good player can beat the field.
+
+## Traps
+- Rivals do not brake for the player (existing traffic AI rule), so they can rear-end a stationary player; tests park the player's car aside before running the field.
+- The wiring test (`test_races_wired_into_the_game`) is vacuous until main.gd makes `game.races`; in this branch it falls back to a standalone node. With the patch applied (checked in a scratch copy) it ran for real, 7 checks.
+- Godot runs share /tmp/godot.lock; never run the full suite from a package.
+- HUD strings stay at 30 characters or less (the race label is 660 px wide at size 26).
+
+## Open
+- Full suite not run here (main session). A shot pass after the patch lands would confirm the HUD prompt in a vehicle.
+- The start prompt shows only within 22 m of the arch; the map marker is the discoverable cue.
+
+## STATUS: PAUSED mid review fixes (2026-10-31, WIP commit)
+Nothing was run after the review-fix edits: no godot command is running or was started in this phase. The last race-test pass line, `152 checks passed, 0 failed` (15 tests, commit df9c56b), is STALE: it predates every item below. The tree may not pass until the tests are finished.
+
+Code written, UNRUN (races.gd, race_course.gd):
+- H1 done in code: `_drop_taken()` (rival whose car is the player's or driver PLAYER is dropped) called in `_go`, the countdown tick and `_update_rivals`.
+- M2 done in code: `_start_block()` and `_offer()` {text, button, act}; `try_interact()` returns start_race's result, so a refused press falls through to exit; notices use button EXIT (in a ride) or ENTER (on foot); starts offered only when `abs(speed) < STOP_SPEED` (3 m/s); `TRIAL_RANGE` 14 (was 30), so a freshly rented bike (a few m from the top) still offers START until it moves.
+- M3 done in code: "Finish the job first" when `game.missions.active`; the race also cancels if a job starts.
+- M4 done in code: `police_sees()` calls the police manager's `_anyone_sees` (prunes freed units first).
+- M5 done in code: `RaceCourse.hill()` adds `runoff` (260 m past the finish) and `runoff_v`; `_spawn_rivals` appends it to each rival line; `_update_rivals` uses `_runoff_throttle` (capped 14 m/s) once `r.finish` is set.
+- Lows done in code: HUD place cached on a 0.25 s tick (`place_runs`); one static beam Shader; night buy-in saved when taken (`_save_now()`); `set_wager` now has a caller (night run: first E opens a 4 s buy-in pick, each further E steps 100/200/300/500, race starts at timeout, driving off cancels); dead `5.4 if i >= 0 else 4.0` removed; burning wrecks go to `_wrecks`, freed by `_sweep_wrecks` only when over 80 m away and out of view.
+
+Tests: HALF-done in race_tests.gd. Done: stand-poor check (button ENTER), night poor case (EXIT, not eaten), night start via `start_race("night")`. NOT done: TESTS list still has the old 15 names; star test (~line 459) still uses `try_interact()` (must be `start_race("night")`) and a fake parked patrol car (rewrite with real frozen cops from `game.police.spawn_cop_at` / `spawn_car_at` with driver NONE); new tests not written: `test_race_player_takes_a_rival_car` (H1), `test_race_press_is_not_eaten` (M2/M3, needs a stub `missions.active` with `check_fail()`), `test_night_race_buy_in_pick`; M5 asserts (runoff non-empty and on roads, rivals more than 40 m past the last gate 6 s after finishing); LOW tests (place_runs, shared shader, stake saved, wreck survives then is freed after the player moves 500 m). race_shots.gd night start still presses E once (now only arms the pick): use `start_race("night")`.
+
+HANDOFF-races.patch: believed current (hud.gd already uses `race_prompt[1]`; player.gd falls through on false), but not re-checked with `git apply --check` after these edits.
+Next, in order: finish tests, add to TESTS, run the race tests under flock (/tmp/R_all.sh, update the ONLY list), fix failures, fix race_shots.gd, `git apply --check`, update this file, commit, report. Leave wip/ alone; the coordinator merges TEST_MODULES by hand.
